    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_title">About %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_body">ConnectHub is an offline-first social blogging app. Every post is stored in an SQLite database on this device, so you can write, edit, search and delete posts without an internet connection.</string>
    <string name="about_features">• Create, edit, view and delete posts offline\n• Save drafts and filter by Draft, Offline or Uploaded\n• Attach a photo from the gallery or camera\n• Search titles and text (partial, case-insensitive)\n• Select several posts to delete or upload together\n• Share a post (text and photo) by email or any app\n• Publish one or many posts to your Blogger blog</string>
    <string name="about_howto">• Swipe a post left to delete (with Undo) or right to edit.\n• Long-press a post to start selecting; use Select all or the X to clear.\n• Open a post and tap Share to email it with its photo.\n• Set up publishing once from Upload → Settings.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">Posts, photos and your profile stay in the app’s private storage. Nothing is uploaded unless you choose Upload. Google sign-in is handled by Google Play services; the app never sees your password and stores no passwords or tokens.</string>
